for key,source,start in [('6686REPORT','EO6686','6. Three months'),('6729COMMITTEE','EO6729','(1) That the Industry'),('6729REPORT','EO6729','(a) That the Industry'),('6601REPORT','EO6601','Within 120 days'),('6271COMMITTEE','EO6271','(1) To effectuate'),('6292AUTHORITY','EO6292','(1) To effectuate'),('6870AREASON','EO6870A','It having been found'),('6870AAMENDMENT','EO6870A','Now, Therefore'),('6870ACOMMISSION','EO6870A','"That there shall be established'),('6756BCOMMISSION','EO6756B','4. That there shall be appointed'),('6861COMMITTEE','EO6861','2. That the National'),('6861TRANSMIT','EO6861','3. That the National'),('6871PERFORMANCE','EO6871','Whereas the National Industrial'),('6871ADOPT','EO6871','Now, Therefore'),('6871REVOKE','EO6871','1. That paragraph'),('6871STAY','EO6871','2. That the effective'),('6871CONTINUE','EO6871','3. That the committee'),('6871PRISON','EO6871','4. That the National'),('6871REPORT','EO6871','5. That on or before'),('7075TRANSFER','EO7075','2. The Administrator'),('7075STUDY','EO7075','3. For the further'),('7076CONTINUE','EO7076','Now, therefore'),('7252TRANSFER','EO7252','2. The Division'),('6320CONSTITUTED','EO6320','By letter of application'),('6543OCOMMITTEE','EO6543O','Applications having'),('6513BSTAY','EO6513B','That all manufacturers'),('6653STAY','EO6653','Now, Therefore'),('6604BSTAY','EO6604B','4. That because'),('6604BREPORT','EO6604B','5. That within')]:excerpt(key,source,start)
prop('A01','An approval condition may be code-dependent, including a reporting requirement: NIRA section 3(a) expressly includes reports and accounts among approval conditions. Its grammatical placement and code-related subject matter are evidence of that relationship, but do not alone establish that all distinct future acts are extinguished by repeal.', ['NIRA3A','SJRES12'],['Do not classify every report as independent merely because it is a report. Conversely, do not classify every study/appointment as extinguished merely because it is inside a code approval.','The separate administrative/research powers and post-repeal orders are counterevidence to a universal subject-matter rule.'],['For each clause identify addressee, required act, authority, relationship to the code, and whether its prospective operation requires code approval/enforcement authority.'])
prop('A02','June 14, 1935 is a supported statutory outer limit for prospective section-3 code approval/prescription/enforcement operation, not proof of the first ending of each command. Title I was selectively extended rather than wholly repealed.', ['SJRES12','SCHECHTERDELEGATION','NIRA2C'],['Schechter on May 27, 1935 must be evaluated as a potential earlier legal endpoint; this worker adopts neither the original shared analysis claim that cancellation is necessary nor a universal May 27 endpoint.','Earlier performance, own terms, supersession and cancellation can precede repeal.'],['Command-specific first-ending inquiry, including effect of Schechter on the particular command and any operative earlier act.'])
prop('A03','Post-repeal research and administrative work was legally contemplated: EO7075 orders analysis/reporting on former codes and transfers eligible Board powers; EO7076 extends consistent existing Title I orders and agencies until April 1, 1936, excluding code approval/prescription/enforcement.', ['NIRA2AB','7075TRANSFER','7075STUDY','7076CONTINUE','7252TRANSFER'],['These texts defeat a universal claim that studying a code necessarily ended June 14, but do not prove continuity of any named earlier committee, report, or unperformed appointment.','EO7252 transfers specified functions/agencies; NRA abolition alone is not proof that every earlier duty ended Jan1 1936.'],['Identify whether the actual auxiliary command was still existing, legally consistent with the amended Act, transferred/continued, cancelled, or performed; no automatic Apr1 endpoint.'])
prop('A04','EO6686 item 6 directs an actual future study submission by the Code Authority, despite appearing among numbered findings. Its three-month term is a due date tied to an effective date, not evidence the study was made or that the command ended.', ['6686REPORT','NIRA3A','7075STUDY'],['The purpose of revising code wages/hours supports code dependence but does not itself demonstrate cancellation of the study obligation.','Approval and study submission require separate treatment.'],['Held code effective date for due-date calculation; actual study/report submission or receipt; later cancellation/transfer or reasoned authority analysis; earlier-ending search.'])
prop('A05','EO6729 has distinct designation/cooperation/recommendation and industry-report duties. Ninety days and December 1, 1934 are deadlines; neither establishes performance. Code-inclusion purposes may limit prospective recommendations but do not prove the committee was created, dissolved, or its report submitted.', ['6729COMMITTEE','6729REPORT','NIRA3A'],['Do not infer extinction from an expired deadline or infer nonperformance from a missing report.','Do not conflate designation of a committee with completion of its investigative/recommendation work.'],['Industry designation, Administrator approval of membership, standards recommendations, industry report/receipt, and any amendment or cancellation, individually tied to the relevant duty.'])
prop('A06','EO6601 is a close comparator to EO6686/6729: its report direction is expressly a condition of approval, concerns code effects and possible revision, and uses a relative deadline. No source-based general distinction found here justifies closing the latter reports by repeal while keeping this one open.', ['6601REPORT','6686REPORT','6729REPORT','NIRA3A'],['This consistency finding does not prove all three survive or all three end together. Different evidence of performance, cancellation, authority or earlier effect may distinguish them.'],['Apply the same clause-level evidentiary questions; secure effective date and actual Administrator report or superseding/cancelling instrument.'])
prop('A07','EO6870A changes the method/size of an existing Commission appointment provision; its recital identifies an inability to agree on a nominee, not completed appointment. The quoted replacement establishes four members to be appointed. The original EO6756B also gives this commission study/recommendation functions.', ['6870AREASON','6870AAMENDMENT','6870ACOMMISSION','6756BCOMMISSION'],['The formal amendment can be distinguished from future appointments and continuing study functions; a change in text does not prove those acts happened.','Do not use the Code Authority nominations as evidence the Board actually appointed members.','The APP slug says 6870 while the project candidate is 6870A; registry identity/custody needs confirmation.'],['Board appointment/constitution record for four-member body; identify which original functions remain after partial replacement; reports/activity/termination; authority and continuation under EO7075/7076 if material.'])
prop('A08','EO6271 and EO6292 creation directions also carry a planning/fair-practice role to cooperate with the Administrator. Their texts do not state an end date. Similarity to EO6870A makes blanket repeal closure of one but not others insufficiently explained.', ['6271COMMITTEE','6292AUTHORITY','6870ACOMMISSION','NIRA2AB'],['Neither the noun committee nor Code Authority conclusively supplies legal authority or lifespan.','Code enforcement functions may end while a performed appointment, records, or a distinct research duty presents a different question.'],['Constitution/member approval, identity of later body, allocated functions and subsequent instruments; separate one-time constitution from continuing activity.'])
prop('A09','EO6871 supplies affirmative evidence that EO6861 committee appointment, hearings, investigation and report actually occurred; the report is dated October 10, 1934. It expressly revokes only EO6861 paragraph 1 and separately continues the committee for further work.', ['6861COMMITTEE','6861TRANSMIT','6871PERFORMANCE','6871ADOPT','6871REVOKE','6871CONTINUE'],['Performance is established for the stated earlier mission, not dissolution of the committee or formal revocation of all of EO6861.','Recital supports appointment by the report date; it does not give the exact appointment date.','President approval of report shows possession by Oct12, but no literal transmission recital establishes exact transmission date.'],['If claiming performance exhaustion, distinguish each act and its proven date/interval: appointment no later than Oct10; report Oct10; presidential possession/consideration no later than Oct12 (inference). Preserve committee continuation and project distinction between functionally spent and formal ending.'])
prop('A10','EO6871 contains separable endpoints and unresolved commands: paragraph1 express revocation on issuance; paragraph2 a stay through December1; paragraphs3-5 continuation/appointment/investigation/report commands with deadlines. The first two cannot close the latter by aggregation.', ['6871REVOKE','6871STAY','6871CONTINUE','6871PRISON','6871REPORT'],['The January15 report is not shown submitted merely because due. Prison Labor Compact study reaches beyond the particular code-amendment suspension; it must not be collapsed into that stay.','Own-terms stay remains subject to intervening modification; stated-date calculation is not exhaustive first-ending research.'],['Separate November15 continuation report, prison-competition committee constitution and Dec1 report, Jan15 Board report, later modifications/cancellations, and authority/transfer analysis.'])
prop('A11','EO6320 is a positive performance lead for EO6292: it expressly describes the Oil Burner Code Authority as duly constituted under article VII and identifies its amendment application dated September29,1933. This establishes that a body so described existed and acted; connecting it to the precise EO6292 creation duty remains necessary.', ['6292AUTHORITY','6320CONSTITUTED'],['Do not assert no constitution evidence exists in the held corpus.','Do not infer all membership-selection requirements, dissolution, or ending of continuing functions from this recital.'],['Held approved code articleVII and membership/appointment record to reconcile identity; if identity established, constitution interval can be bounded by approval and dated application while ongoing functions remain separately open.'],'new held positive evidence lead')
prop('A12','EO6543O names applications by a Wall Paper Executive Committee on September27 and October7,1933. This is an activity/identity lead, weaker than EO6320: the excerpt does not say it is the exact eight-member planning agency required by EO6271.', ['6271COMMITTEE','6543OCOMMITTEE'],['Same industry and similar name do not establish identical body or completed composition.'],['Approved code articleXIV and committee constitution/membership records; application itself or Administrator report connecting the bodies.'],'new held activity lead')
prop('A13','EO6513B and EO6653 stays directly suspend application of code provisions pending an Administrator determination/order. Their code-dependent prospective function cannot outlive effective operation of the suspended code, but no held later determination found in this bounded search establishes their first end.', ['6513BSTAY','6653STAY','NIRA3A','SJRES12'],['No later record found is not proof no determination occurred.','A condition defining the stay does not necessarily impose an independent duty to issue a determination; read the actual words.','June14 is at most a statutory outside bound, with Schechter and earlier administrative action unresolved.'],['Actual Administrator determination/further order and effective date, code amendment/supersession/cancellation; distinguish the stayed provision from any separate directed act.'])
prop('A14','EO6604B demonstrates why one order needs clause separation: paragraph4 suspends a provision pending investigation/report/further order, while paragraph5 permits hearings within ninety days and thereafter directs a report. The wording does not support a simple statement that paragraph5 requires the report within ninety days.', ['6604BSTAY','6604BREPORT'],['A permissive hearing authorization and mandatory subsequent report are not identical commands.','No assertion is made that the dependent trigger occurred or that the report obligation never arose.'],['Code effective date, hearings and notice record, report, Administrator investigation/order, and any cancellation or replacement.'])
